WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.766 --> 00:00:08.233
- Hey, Professor Sycamore.
- It's really good to see you, Ash.

2
00:00:08.666 --> 00:00:11.333
- We want you to check something out.
- Pika, Pika.

3
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.233
Here, look.

4
00:00:12.866 --> 00:00:16.433
We just discovered it the other day, but it's not listed in the Pokédex.

5
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.966
So, we figured you might know what it is.

6
00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.033
Hmm.

7
00:00:20.866 --> 00:00:22.600
That is a new one to me.

8
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.966
And you couldn't find it in the Pokédex?

9
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.200
I wonder if it might be a new kind.

10
00:00:27.266 --> 00:00:31.033
- Huh? You really think it could be?
- If it is, that's amazing.

11
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:31.933
Mm-hm.

12
00:00:32.366 --> 00:00:35.033
Could you turn it around so I could see it from all sides?

13
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.400
Okay. Ooh.

14
00:00:37.866 --> 00:00:40.300
He's talking about Squishy, not you.

15
00:00:40.366 --> 00:00:41.800
Oops. I didn't know.

16
00:00:45.866 --> 00:00:47.466
Hmm.

17
00:00:47.533 --> 00:00:48.966
I've never seen it before.

18
00:00:49.733 --> 00:00:53.333
It feels really squishy. That's why I named it Squishy.

19
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.700
I'll look into it on my end.

20
00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:01.366
If I find anything out, I'll let you know. In the meantime, keep an eye on Squishy.

21
00:01:01.433 --> 00:01:02.600
Sure, got it.

22
00:01:03.166 --> 00:01:04.400
So cute.

23
00:01:04.466 --> 00:01:05.800
They call it Squishy.

24
00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:08.500
It's the Pokémon those red suits called Z.

25
00:01:08.566 --> 00:01:12.100
It's gotta be big news if they reported it to Professor Sycamore.

26
00:01:12.533 --> 00:01:14.466
So, if it's a new kind of Pokémon,

27
00:01:14.533 --> 00:01:17.300
does that mean we'll get to give it a name once we catch it?

28
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.066
Like "Beautiful Jess"?

29
00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.400
Or "Meowth Junior."

30
00:01:20.466 --> 00:01:22.266
"Cool James" has a certain ring.

31
00:01:23.766 --> 00:01:25.600
- And now, tally-ho.
- Let's go.

32
00:01:25.666 --> 00:01:28.233
Wobba!

33
00:01:32.533 --> 00:01:33.400
Huh?

34
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.400
I think Squishy likes to be in there, too.

35
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.166
What should I do?

36
00:01:45.933 --> 00:01:48.233
I know. Just leave it to me.

37
00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.866
I'll make your bag way better.

38
00:01:50.666 --> 00:01:53.400
- You will? Yay!
- Yay!

39
00:01:58.933 --> 00:02:02.300
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

40
00:02:03.066 --> 00:02:06.233
♪ Knock me down I'll just get up again ♪

41
00:02:06.766 --> 00:02:10.133
♪ You've met your match Yeah, I'm no beginner ♪

42
00:02:10.199 --> 00:02:12.800
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

43
00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.366
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

44
00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:17.700
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

45
00:02:17.766 --> 00:02:20.933
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

46
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.666
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

47
00:02:33.366 --> 00:02:36.533
Our heroes continue their journey to the Snowbelle City Gym,

48
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:38.933
where Ash hopes to win his eighth gym badge

49
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.133
and enter the Kalos League.

50
00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:12.700
- Huh?
- Squishy sure loves the sun, doesn't it?

51
00:03:17.766 --> 00:03:21.233
I wouldn't be surprised if Squishy's actually converting sunlight

52
00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.366
to use as energy.

53
00:03:22.433 --> 00:03:23.700
Oh, yeah.

54
00:03:29.633 --> 00:03:32.300
So, Squishy must absorb sunlight instead of eating.

55
00:03:32.366 --> 00:03:33.566
Ah.

56
00:03:36.933 --> 00:03:38.466
Sunlight for food?

57
00:03:38.533 --> 00:03:40.800
So, it lives on an empty stomach.

58
00:03:40.866 --> 00:03:42.733
What a curious little Pokémon.

59
00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.700
If we research that rascal,

60
00:03:44.766 --> 00:03:48.100
maybe we can figure out how to cut out needing grub, too.

61
00:03:48.166 --> 00:03:49.166
No food?

62
00:03:49.233 --> 00:03:50.333
How economical.

63
00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.133
But that means there'll be no more yummy chocolate cake for me.

64
00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.700
Yeah. No dessert.

65
00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:59.300
So, Operation Squishy Catch is sure to place us

66
00:03:59.366 --> 00:04:01.733
in the Team Rocket legends category.

67
00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.066
Yes, ma'am.

68
00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.633
How does it feel? You like it?

69
00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:07.566
Eevee!

70
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.766
It seems like Eevee's starting to get used to everyone.

71
00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:13.300
Yeah. Eevee's working hard on that.

72
00:04:13.966 --> 00:04:15.066
Huh?

73
00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:17.266
Quilladin, din, din!

74
00:04:17.766 --> 00:04:20.033
Ta-da! It's all finished.

75
00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.766
Courtesy of yours truly. A special space just for Squishy.

76
00:04:23.833 --> 00:04:25.866
Yay! That's awesome.

77
00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:28.366
Thanks a lot, Serena.

78
00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:32.166
- Squishy, look at this.
- Dedenne!

79
00:04:32.233 --> 00:04:33.333
Ooh!

80
00:04:34.566 --> 00:04:36.200
You solved that problem.

81
00:04:36.266 --> 00:04:38.300
That's really nice of you, Serena.

82
00:04:38.366 --> 00:04:39.866
I'm glad I could help.

83
00:04:39.933 --> 00:04:41.866
I sure hope both of them are happy.

84
00:04:42.366 --> 00:04:45.166
Hey, Serena, they really like it a whole lot.

85
00:04:45.233 --> 00:04:47.666
- Dedenne!
- Mm!

86
00:04:47.733 --> 00:04:49.000
Thank goodness.

87
00:04:50.366 --> 00:04:53.500
Okay, Eevee, let's go practice for the next showcase.

88
00:04:54.066 --> 00:04:55.233
Eevee!

89
00:05:00.766 --> 00:05:02.633
Eevee!

90
00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.733
- Great. You're so good.
- Eevee!

91
00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.300
-Huh?

92
00:05:13.866 --> 00:05:17.900
Quilladin, din, din, din!

93
00:05:17.966 --> 00:05:19.466
Eevee!

94
00:05:20.866 --> 00:05:22.600
Eevee, you okay?

95
00:05:23.166 --> 00:05:25.100
Never seen that Pokémon before.

96
00:05:25.933 --> 00:05:27.966
Quilladin. The Spiny Armor Pokémon

97
00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:29.833
and the evolved form of Chespin.

98
00:05:30.266 --> 00:05:33.000
The hard shell covering Quilladin's body is so tough

99
00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:35.933
a direct hit from a large truck wouldn't even dent it.

100
00:05:36.333 --> 00:05:39.033
Quilladin uses this shell to deflect foes' attacks,

101
00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.433
and it strikes back with its sharp quills.

102
00:05:42.833 --> 00:05:45.733
- Chespin evolves into that?
- Dedenne.

103
00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:50.400
Quilladin, din, din, din!

104
00:05:51.633 --> 00:05:53.966
Its vine whip's in the shape of a heart.

105
00:05:54.033 --> 00:05:57.033
Does that mean Quilladin has fallen in love with Eevee?

106
00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.666
Whoa! Love at first sight?

107
00:06:02.633 --> 00:06:05.033
Ladin, din, din, din!

108
00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:06.566
Now it's using rollout.

109
00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.066
What do we do?

110
00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:11.200
I don't know. We can't tell it not to be in love.

111
00:06:11.266 --> 00:06:12.366
- Pancham!
- Huh?

112
00:06:17.533 --> 00:06:19.200
- Pancham?
- Chespin, too?

113
00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:34.566
Eevee!

114
00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.633
Eevee!

115
00:06:48.666 --> 00:06:51.133
Oh, man, that Pokémon's out of control.

116
00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.233
Could that be the end of the battle?

117
00:06:53.333 --> 00:06:56.633
It wasn't actually an attack, but Quilladin got knocked down.

118
00:06:57.066 --> 00:06:59.166
Anyhow, I'm glad Eevee's okay.

119
00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:05.933
- Eevee?

120
00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:16.800
Quilladin, din. Huh?

121
00:07:16.866 --> 00:07:18.700
Hey. It woke up.

122
00:07:18.766 --> 00:07:21.333
- You okay?
- Pikachu.

123
00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:23.300
- Quilladin.
- Huh? You're welcome.

124
00:07:23.366 --> 00:07:26.100
- It does know how to be polite.
- Eevee.

125
00:07:26.166 --> 00:07:27.966
- Quill!
- It's leaving.

126
00:07:28.633 --> 00:07:30.966
Huh. How strange.

127
00:07:31.033 --> 00:07:32.700
Do you think maybe it gave up?

128
00:07:32.766 --> 00:07:34.800
Nope, because it's coming back.

129
00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.800
Now it's bringing flowers to Eevee.

130
00:07:37.866 --> 00:07:39.133
What do you know?

131
00:07:40.133 --> 00:07:41.233
Quilladin.

132
00:07:45.066 --> 00:07:46.766
Eevee's not interested.

133
00:07:46.833 --> 00:07:51.200
Uh... I want Eevee to make friends with all sorts of Pokémon,

134
00:07:51.266 --> 00:07:52.833
but I'm not sure about this.

135
00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:04.533
Oh, boy.

136
00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:06.400
Enough with the fighting already.

137
00:08:06.966 --> 00:08:09.133
I doubt this is going to be resolved.

138
00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:12.400
Well, acting like a bully isn't the way to anybody's heart.

139
00:08:15.933 --> 00:08:17.033
Huh?

140
00:08:18.733 --> 00:08:19.866
Eevee.

141
00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:27.633
- Quilladin, din, din, din!
- Pancham.

142
00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:33.966
Hey. What's Quilladin doing now?

143
00:08:34.033 --> 00:08:36.200
I think it wants to have a battle with Pancham.

144
00:08:36.266 --> 00:08:37.933
Whoa, it's picking a fight again.

145
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.466
What's going on?

146
00:08:39.533 --> 00:08:43.900
I think Quilladin wants to show Eevee how strong it is by battling with Pancham.

147
00:08:43.966 --> 00:08:46.433
Of course. It just wants to show off.

148
00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:51.233
Maybe, but I don't think Eevee would like someone who would do such a thing.

149
00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:55.600
Pancham? What do you say?

150
00:09:08.933 --> 00:09:13.000
Huh? Oh, Eevee feels more comfortable when it's close to Bunnelby.

151
00:09:13.633 --> 00:09:15.766
Quilladin.

152
00:09:15.833 --> 00:09:17.800
Good luck to both of you.

153
00:09:17.866 --> 00:09:19.000
Pika!

154
00:09:27.433 --> 00:09:28.700
Quick, dodge it!

155
00:09:30.066 --> 00:09:31.266
Stone edge!

156
00:09:31.333 --> 00:09:33.966
Pancham!

157
00:09:40.766 --> 00:09:41.766
Dodge it!

158
00:09:45.466 --> 00:09:47.300
-Dark pulse, go!

159
00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:55.666
It's fine.

160
00:09:55.733 --> 00:09:57.933
Wow, needle arm for a last-second block.

161
00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.266
Arm thrust!

162
00:10:01.566 --> 00:10:02.566
Are you all right?

163
00:10:03.433 --> 00:10:04.400
Pancham.

164
00:10:05.066 --> 00:10:06.633
Quilladin!

165
00:10:11.133 --> 00:10:12.733
Quilladin!

166
00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:14.300
Now you wanna battle Chespin?

167
00:10:22.966 --> 00:10:24.900
Yay! Go, Chespin, go!

168
00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:34.500
Dodge it, quick!

169
00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:36.800
Tackle, let's go!

170
00:10:41.166 --> 00:10:42.433
Chespin, Chespin!

171
00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:45.433
That Quilladin's really fast for its size.

172
00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:46.766
Pika, Pika.

173
00:10:46.833 --> 00:10:48.000
Pin missile!

174
00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:58.633
Not a scratch.

175
00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:01.200
- Quilladin's shell is tough.
- Pika.

176
00:11:01.733 --> 00:11:03.000
Keep your distance!

177
00:11:07.333 --> 00:11:11.133
Quill.

178
00:11:14.766 --> 00:11:15.766
Hmm?

179
00:11:17.166 --> 00:11:19.333
-Hmm?

180
00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.500
Huh?

181
00:11:44.933 --> 00:11:47.366
Quilladin. Huh?

182
00:11:49.666 --> 00:11:51.366
- Eevee!
- Squishy!

183
00:11:51.433 --> 00:11:52.600
- Bunnelby!
- Dedenne!

184
00:11:52.666 --> 00:11:54.100
Hey, what's going on?

185
00:11:54.833 --> 00:11:56.800
Prepare for trouble we stir up so well.

186
00:11:56.866 --> 00:11:59.100
And make it double, that's where I excel.

187
00:11:59.166 --> 00:12:01.666
To protect the world from dumb Pokémon names.

188
00:12:01.733 --> 00:12:04.366
To unite Team Rocket with fortunes and fames.

189
00:12:04.433 --> 00:12:07.166
To denounce all the boredom that you twerps create.

190
00:12:07.566 --> 00:12:10.166
To extend our names, thus sealing our fate.

191
00:12:10.966 --> 00:12:12.733
- Jessie.
- And James.

192
00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:16.166
Team Rocket blasts off as creatively as ever.

193
00:12:16.233 --> 00:12:19.133
When we name a Pokémon, it's a permanent endeavor.

194
00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:20.833
Meowth, I'm clever!

195
00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:24.066
Team Rocket!

196
00:12:24.133 --> 00:12:26.966
Operation Fake Squishy is a success.

197
00:12:27.033 --> 00:12:29.533
We'll take all these Pokémon and leave you a mess.

198
00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:30.566
What a haul!

199
00:12:30.633 --> 00:12:31.500
Have a ball.

200
00:12:31.566 --> 00:12:32.533
Stop!

201
00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:37.100
- Huh?
- Pika?

202
00:12:38.566 --> 00:12:40.533
Talonflame. Noibat.

203
00:12:42.233 --> 00:12:44.800
Go and find Team Rocket's balloon, okay?

204
00:12:44.866 --> 00:12:46.800
They couldn't have gotten too far away.

205
00:12:56.666 --> 00:12:57.766
What are you doing?

206
00:12:58.233 --> 00:13:00.600
Let's go look for them, too.

207
00:13:00.666 --> 00:13:01.700
- Right.
- Okay, Ash.

208
00:13:07.066 --> 00:13:08.933
Who's that Pokémon?

209
00:13:14.066 --> 00:13:15.900
It's Quilladin!

210
00:13:15.966 --> 00:13:17.166
Quilladin!

211
00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:37.233
Huh?

212
00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:39.233
Bunnelby.

213
00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:47.233
- Dedenne!
- Eevee.

214
00:13:58.266 --> 00:13:59.233
Eevee!

215
00:14:01.866 --> 00:14:05.133
All right, who's going to name our greenish friend?

216
00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:06.100
I caught it.

217
00:14:06.166 --> 00:14:07.666
I get to name it, right?

218
00:14:07.733 --> 00:14:10.800
No way. Any achievement of yours is mine, as well.

219
00:14:10.866 --> 00:14:12.966
Team Rocket should get the credit, dig?

220
00:14:13.033 --> 00:14:14.233
Oh, please.

221
00:14:14.366 --> 00:14:16.800
Right, Beautiful Jess? Huh?

222
00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:21.300
They're gone, without a trace!

223
00:14:21.366 --> 00:14:22.766
Meowth, turn back.

224
00:14:22.833 --> 00:14:23.733
Aye, aye, chief.

225
00:14:24.433 --> 00:14:28.066
We'll recatch them all, including my Beautiful Jessie.

226
00:14:29.733 --> 00:14:32.233
- Talonflame.
- Noibat.

227
00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.300
Find them?

228
00:14:33.366 --> 00:14:35.100
- Talon.
- Noibat.

229
00:14:35.166 --> 00:14:36.266
Then keep looking.

230
00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:51.133
Hey! Stop fighting!

231
00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:52.133
Chespin.

232
00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.633
Pancham, you, too.

233
00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:55.133
There's no time for that.

234
00:14:57.400 --> 00:15:00.900
Hey, we all need to work together if we're gonna rescue our friends.

235
00:15:00.966 --> 00:15:02.166
Huh?

236
00:15:07.466 --> 00:15:08.366
Huh?

237
00:15:08.433 --> 00:15:09.700
How rude to run away.

238
00:15:09.766 --> 00:15:12.133
Right. Now hand Cool James over.

239
00:15:16.433 --> 00:15:18.366
Teach them some manners, Gourgeist.

240
00:15:18.433 --> 00:15:20.000
Inkay, join the fray!

241
00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:26.466
Bunnelby!

242
00:15:28.633 --> 00:15:29.633
Use tackle.

243
00:15:36.733 --> 00:15:39.066
Show them your shadow ball!

244
00:15:47.133 --> 00:15:48.400
Eevee!

245
00:15:48.933 --> 00:15:51.800
Bunnelby!

246
00:15:52.233 --> 00:15:53.266
Use dark pulse.

247
00:15:58.000 --> 00:15:59.933
Now, time to use seed bomb.

248
00:16:10.033 --> 00:16:12.200
Good. No more interruptions.

249
00:16:12.266 --> 00:16:15.033
Come to Jessie, Beautiful Jess.

250
00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:16.666
No, it's Meowth Junior.

251
00:16:16.733 --> 00:16:18.300
Ignore them. You're Cool James.

252
00:16:18.366 --> 00:16:20.600
Come on. That sounds like a hippie's name.

253
00:16:20.666 --> 00:16:21.500
Whatever.

254
00:16:21.566 --> 00:16:26.166
If we hand over that Pokémon to the boss, our bonus points will really pile up.

255
00:16:26.966 --> 00:16:29.766
- Noibat!
- Oh, no.

256
00:16:29.833 --> 00:16:30.966
We found you.

257
00:16:32.066 --> 00:16:33.533
Twerpish timing.

258
00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:34.833
Twerps stink.

259
00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:36.333
- Inkay.
- Gourgeist.

260
00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:37.966
Squishy, Dedenne!

261
00:16:38.033 --> 00:16:39.633
Oh, Eevee, are you okay?

262
00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:41.166
I'm proud of you, Bunnelby.

263
00:16:41.233 --> 00:16:43.366
You crooks won't get away with this!

264
00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:51.200
- Man, oh, man.
- Pika, Pikachu.

265
00:16:58.166 --> 00:17:01.600
We all need to work together if we're gonna rescue our friends.

266
00:17:06.099 --> 00:17:07.633
Blah, blah. Translation?

267
00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:09.200
They're calling a truce.

268
00:17:09.266 --> 00:17:12.933
The big guy says they should all work together to protect their pals.

269
00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:14.166
How mature.

270
00:17:18.833 --> 00:17:19.933
That's awesome.

271
00:17:22.633 --> 00:17:25.266
What? You want to have at it with us?

272
00:17:25.333 --> 00:17:27.866
Then, okay, Inkay. Use psybeam!

273
00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:31.066
Quilladin.

274
00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:39.566
Why, you...

275
00:17:39.633 --> 00:17:41.400
All right, use tackle.

276
00:17:45.533 --> 00:17:47.700
- Quilladin!
- Pancham!

277
00:17:47.766 --> 00:17:48.933
Brats.

278
00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.800
Gourgeist, use seed bomb!

279
00:17:57.100 --> 00:17:58.666
Great teamwork. Good job.

280
00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.666
Chespin!

281
00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:27.266
We're blasting off again!

282
00:18:27.333 --> 00:18:28.766
Inkay.

283
00:18:31.433 --> 00:18:33.266
Bye-bye.

284
00:18:33.333 --> 00:18:36.033
You know what? You worked really great together.

285
00:18:36.533 --> 00:18:37.966
You should be proud of yourselves.

286
00:18:38.566 --> 00:18:41.300
- Pancham, cham.
- Quilladin.

287
00:18:41.366 --> 00:18:42.633
Chespin, Ches.

288
00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:44.133
Din, din.

289
00:18:47.166 --> 00:18:48.766
Hmm? Huh?

290
00:18:50.333 --> 00:18:52.000
Huh? Quilladin?

291
00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:54.733
Huh?

292
00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:57.633
Look, it's coming back.

293
00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.533
Quilla...

294
00:19:01.833 --> 00:19:02.933
..din!

295
00:19:11.533 --> 00:19:13.833
Oh! I'm sorry, Quilladin.

296
00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:17.900
It's not because Eevee doesn't like you or anything like that.

297
00:19:18.433 --> 00:19:22.100
It's just very shy, so, opening up isn't easy.

298
00:19:36.833 --> 00:19:38.733
At least they're getting along now.

299
00:19:38.800 --> 00:19:41.433
I doubt Quilladin was trying to win them over.

300
00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:43.966
-Huh?

301
00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:55.333
Quill... Quilladin! Din, din, din!

302
00:19:56.766 --> 00:19:57.933
Quilladin!

303
00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:03.066
- Pancham.
- Chespin, pin.

304
00:20:04.466 --> 00:20:06.366
Well, that was a quick turnaround.

305
00:20:06.833 --> 00:20:08.733
Guess we were worrying for nothing.

306
00:20:09.333 --> 00:20:12.733
Okay, back to work on the Pokémon Showcase.

307
00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:13.733
Eevee!

308
00:20:14.566 --> 00:20:17.766
Yeah. Training sounds good, right, buddy?

309
00:20:18.333 --> 00:20:19.500
Pika!

310
00:20:20.266 --> 00:20:23.233
Hey, Bonnie, how about we make some lunch while they're all busy?

311
00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:25.500
Mm-hm. I'm so hungry.

312
00:20:25.966 --> 00:20:27.233
What can I do?

313
00:20:27.300 --> 00:20:28.966
You could go get us some water.

314
00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:30.433
Okay.

315
00:20:32.533 --> 00:20:35.100
Some friendships end up going one way,

316
00:20:35.166 --> 00:20:37.266
and some end up going another.

317
00:20:37.333 --> 00:20:40.933
So, after saying goodbye to a newly distracted Quilladin,

318
00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:43.866
our heroes' journey continues.
